From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: the guest's /proc/self/map_files leaves out the host's own files

/proc/self/map_files has one entry per file-backed mapping, named by its range; reading an entry's link gives the mapped file. Tencent
ACE in PGR opens the directory, lists it and reads every link (6001 readlinks in one run, traced with bpftrace on RunGuestSyscall):
that named the translator, the JVM and the x86_64 host libraries (1200 links into /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu alone), although 0012
keeps them out of its /proc/self/maps. The guest's view now leaves those entries out: getdents64 on its own map_files directory
drops the entries whose file is host-only, and readlinkat of such an entry (absolute or relative to that directory) fails with
ENOENT. A device's process has no entry for an anonymous mapping, and 0012 prints these mappings as anonymous. A batch filtered to
nothing is not returned empty (that reads as the end of the directory): the next batch is fetched.
The host-only rules move from 0012's maps code into IsHostOnlyMappedFile (code cache memfd, host GPU nodes, host system directories,
the JVM's data files, ELF files for another machine than aarch64), shared by both views; 0012's output is unchanged (checked over
PGR's real maps). BERBERIS_SHOW_HOST_MAPS turns both off. Applies after 0011 and 0012. Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/kernel_api/arm64/gen_syscall_emulation_arm64_to_x86_64-inl.h b/kernel_api/arm64/gen_syscall_emulation_arm64_to_x86_64-inl.h
